  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion-domain:pbps-hilbert-corrector-perturbation",
    "anchor": "PBPS B20 and Appendix B4 Ex28--Ex34 perturbation algebra; future actual B27/B28 adapter",
    "original_text": "Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang, arXiv:2609.06905v1, B20 and Lemma B4 perturbation expansion Ex28–Ex34. ASTIS auxiliary real Hilbert generalization with all structural assumptions explicit; not a verbatim source theorem.\nLet H be a complete real Hilbert space, allowing the zero space. Let A,G,Inv:H→H be bounded real-linear endomorphisms. Assume A,G,Inv are selfadjoint, A commutes with Inv, Inv G=G Inv=I, and A²+G²=I. Every one of these structural conditions is an explicit hypothesis of this auxiliary algebra theorem. For arbitrary u,v,r∈H define C(a,b)=(||a||²−||b||²)/2−⟨A(Inv a),b⟩. Then C(u+Gr,v−Ar)−C(u,v)=⟨u,Inv r⟩+||r||²/2. The half, plus sign, operator order and same three operators are exact. This is an ASTIS Hilbert-space auxiliary generalization of the algebra in Chen–Chewi–Lu–Zhang's PBPS B20 and Lemma B4 expansion Ex28–Ex34, rather than a claim that the paper states a theorem for arbitrary Hilbert operators. No positivity, finite dimension, spectral gap, surjectivity or probability hypothesis is needed by this algebra identity. The actual PBPS consumer constructs all seven operator facts internally on its same centered space. Arbitrary r is not yet the paper's r_rho; the actual H/K/B27 adapter and B4/B28 decay proof remain open.\nPBPS B20 and Appendix B4 Ex28--Ex34 perturbation algebra; future actual B27/B28 adapter",
    "text_sha256": "50d5746c4b5c9297143d13ea79d382d2924b17e76a187201c932c21cb5201724"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.HilbertCorrectorPerturbation.quadratic_corrector_perturbation",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Analysis/HilbertCorrectorPerturbation.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H]\n    [CompleteSpace H]\n    (A G Inv : H →L[ℝ] H)\n    (hA : IsSelfAdjoint A) (hG : IsSelfAdjoint G)\n    (hInv : IsSelfAdjoint Inv) (hAInv : Commute A Inv)\n    (hInvG : Inv * G = 1) (hGInv : G * Inv = 1)\n    (hSquares : A * A + G * G = 1)\n    (u v r : H) :\n    let C : H → H → ℝ := fun u v =>\n      (‖u‖^2 - ‖v‖^2)/2 - inner ℝ (A (Inv u)) v\n    C (u + G r) (v - A r) - C u v =\n      inner ℝ u (Inv r) + ‖r‖^2/2",
    "statement_sha256": "1922c937bb5bd3434472d6c3080cc027e7f7acc07dec47010fce978cacbeba89",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "For every complete real Hilbert space H (also allowing the zero space), every three bounded real-linear endomorphisms A, G, Inv of H, and every u,v,r in H, suppose A, G, and Inv are selfadjoint; A commutes with Inv; Inv composed with G and G composed with Inv both equal the identity; and A composed with A plus G composed with G equals the identity. Define, for every a,b in H,\nC(a,b) = (||a||² - ||b||²)/2 - <A(Inv(a)),b>.\nThen\nC(u+G(r), v-A(r)) - C(u,v) = <u,Inv(r)> + ||r||²/2.\nThe function C is locally defined from the already quantified A and Inv. Its two argument names do not rebind the theorem's fixed u,v outside the function. The conclusion is an exact real identity for every triple u,v,r, with no positivity, nonzero-dimension, scalar-parameter, or probabilistic premise.",
    "text_sha256": "7fb468c27c8165adc6d80d2ca720da55937ecd38e4a7c7704637a7d09168ea16",
    "decoder": "anonymous_decoder72",
    "decoder_packet_sha256": "67bc6e7f76d2e537f13d061d5139982898fbb204727b83fd77fb7451183bedbf",
    "decoder_run_sha256": "23b058be5d13493b869e9b1966e00552bdef6b3e77db2124b5d764e61d7d7948",
    "source_text_visible": false
  },
