          "text": "Move A and Inv through the inner products and apply the preceding vector identity with x=r. Thus the sum of the two surviving u-linear terms is exactly the claimed right-hand linear term.",
          "formula": "\\langle A\\operatorname{Inv}u,Ar\\rangle+\\langle u,Gr\\rangle=\\langle u,\\operatorname{Inv}r\\rangle.",
          "lean": "  have hMixed : inner ℝ (A (Inv u)) (A r)+inner ℝ u (G r)=inner ℝ u (Inv r) := by\n    rw [ha (Inv u) (A r),hi u (A (A r)),\n      ← inner_add_right,hLinear r]\n",
